7... cxd4 8. exd4 Nc6
{ We arrive at a reverse Tarash position where white has an extra tempo. } 9.
h3
{ A useful move - preventing Bg4 which is usually an important idea in IQP positions to attack the knight covering the d4 pawn. By playing h3, white robs black of access to the g4 square. This is inspired by the move h6 used by Magnus Carlsen in similar positions. }
